  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl, combine the sugar, flour, baking powder, salt, dates and nuts. Add the eggs, butter and vanilla; stir just until dry ingredients are moistened (batter will be very stiff).",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread in a greased 15-in. x 10-in. x 1-in. baking pan. Bake at 350 degrees F for 20-25 minutes or until golden brown. Cool bars on a wire rack. Dust with confectioners' sugar. Bars will keep well stored in airtight containers in the freezer.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "Feel free to add raisins and/or coconut. Recipe is very flexible. Try cutting down sugar to 1 and ½ cups. Also, bars are sweet enough without powdered sugar."
